# Keep the TAS2781 smart amp powered so its DSP program stays resident.
#
# The amp runtime-suspends 3s after the speakers go idle and drops its program;
# the driver only reloads it from the playback hook, so the next stream races
# that reload and sometimes loses. When it loses, the sink, the active port, the
# Speaker/Headphone switches and every volume read correct and nothing comes out
# — which is indistinguishable from working audio until you notice the silence.
#
# starch-speaker-rearm still exists for the manual case, but it only ever fired
# on a headphone-jack event, and the idle suspend happens whether or not
# headphones are involved. Pinning runtime PM removes the race instead of
# reacting to it: no suspend, no dropped program, nothing to lose.
#
# Costs the amp's idle draw, which is why this is a rule and not a default.
# Match on the driver rather than the ACPI id so other TAS2781 machines are
# covered; the KERNEL match is the fallback for when the bind event beats the
# driver link being readable. "change" is included so a udevadm trigger
# reapplies the pin to the device that is already present, without a reboot.
ACTION=="add|bind|change", SUBSYSTEM=="i2c", DRIVER=="tas2781-hda", ATTR{power/control}="on"
ACTION=="add|bind|change", SUBSYSTEM=="i2c", KERNEL=="i2c-TIAS2781:*", ATTR{power/control}="on"
